tuxdisplay (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add native OpenDisplay protocol v3 streaming over usbmuxd.
  * Stream low-latency H.264 directly to the App Store receiver on TCP 9000.
  * Support USB operation without IP networking, Internet, or Personal Hotspot.
  * Forward OpenDisplay touch, scroll, and Pencil input into GNOME Wayland.
  * Keep the authenticated Safari/browser transport as a compatibility fallback.

 -- Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0200

tuxdisplay (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a standalone GTK manager with an automatically started tray indicator.
  * Show disconnected, running, and actively connected tray states.
  * Add tray and manager actions to close the display connection.
  * Detect trusted iPads and ipheth addresses for USB cable connections.
  * Guide iPad tethering and retain device-port USB gadget support.

 -- Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:30:00 +0200

tuxdisplay (0.2.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pin the GNOME virtual monitor to the configured display mode.
  * Stop the user service cleanly using the daemon interrupt path.

 -- Tomas Pluharik <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:45:00 +0200

tuxdisplay (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix frozen display by sending absolute pointer and touch input to the
    ScreenCast object path required by Mutter.
  * Bound service shutdown so upgrades cannot leave a stale stream process.

 -- TuxDisplay contributors <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0200

